---
description: |
  Synchronizes indicators of compromise (IOCs) of one type into an IOC source
  of a HarfangLab Manager and returns one result event per indicator.

  Every input event holds one indicator in `value`. The operator collects the
  whole input before it sends any request, so the input must end, for example
  one snapshot of a feed inside `every`. It looks up the source by name and
  creates it if it doesn't exist. Then it reads the IOCs of `type` in the
  source once and compares them with the input. Only differences cause
  requests: it creates missing IOCs, changes the state of IOCs whose state
  differs, updates IOCs whose description, comment, level, or confidence
  differs, and leaves the others unchanged. A run with the same input sends no
  write request.

  The operator owns the IOCs of `type` in the source and reverts manual
  changes on the next run, for example an IOC that an analyst disabled in the
  console while the feed still lists it. Use a source that only the operator
  writes to.

  State changes and deletions go out first, in bulk requests of up to 1,000
  IOCs. The Manager has no bulk route for creating IOCs or for changing their
  content, so every creation and content update is one request, with up to
  `parallel` requests at a time per instance of the operator. One such
  request takes about a second on the Manager, so the first run of a feed
  takes long: about 40 minutes for 10,000 IOCs and 4 to 7 hours for 100,000
  IOCs at `parallel=8`. Changing `label`, `level`, or `confidence` later
  updates every IOC of the source and takes as long.

  Don't load a feed with the Manager's CSV import instead. The import creates
  IOCs in the `block` state, regardless of the state of the source, and the
  operator doesn't use it.

  Domains and hashes are lowercased, and IP addresses are sent in their
  canonical form, because the Manager stores them as sent. A value that isn't
  valid for `type`, such as a subnet for `ip` or a hash of the wrong length,
  yields a `failed` result and isn't sent. Values match case-insensitively, as
  on the Manager. When the input holds a value more than once, an active row
  wins over a revoked or expired one, and the first spelling and the first
  description in sort order win.

  An indicator whose `expires` lies in the past or whose `revoked` is `true`
  is disabled, or deleted with `on_revoke="delete"`. With `prune=true`, the
  operator also disables the IOCs of `type` in the source that the input no
  longer contains. An input without valid indicators changes nothing, even
  with `prune=true`. To protect against a truncated or wrong feed, a run stops
  before any write when pruning would disable more than `max_prune` IOCs and
  more than `max_prune_share` of the active IOCs of `type` in the source.

  The run also stops before any write when the listing of the source fails,
  or returns fewer or more IOCs than it counts. Such an error ends the
  pipeline, including a surrounding `every`, so watch the pipeline state. A
  failed write doesn't stop the run.

  The result events have the shape `{value, type, action, ioc_id, error}`,
  where `action` is `created`, `updated`, `unchanged`, `disabled`, `deleted`,
  `skipped`, or `failed`. A `failed` result holds the reason or the Manager's
  response in `error`, so watch for these results to notice rejected
  indicators. `skipped` marks a revoked or expired indicator that the source
  doesn't contain. IOCs that already are disabled and are missing from the
  input produce no result. With `dry_run=true`, the results show what a run
  would do, without any write.

  The operator holds the input and the IOCs of the source in memory. A run
  with 100,000 indicators took about 1.4 GB against a mock Manager.
args:
  positional:
    - name: url
      type: string
      description: |
        Base URL of the Manager API, for example
        `https://example.hurukai.io:8443`.
  named:
    - name: token
      type: secret
      description: |
        API token of a HarfangLab user, without the `Token` prefix. The user
        needs to view and edit threat intelligence.
    - name: source
      type: string
      description: Name of the IOC source to synchronize.
    - name: type
      type: string
      description: |
        Type of the indicators: `domain`, `ip`, `sha256`, `sha1`, `md5`,
        `filename`, `filepath`, or `url`. `ip` maps to destination IP
        addresses. The hash types share the HarfangLab type `hash`; the
        operator tells them apart by their length, so that the runs of
        different hash types don't touch each other's IOCs.
    - name: value
      type: field
      description: Field with the indicator value.
    - name: description
      type: field
      default: null
      description: Field with a description of the indicator.
    - name: expires
      type: field
      default: null
      description: |
        Field with the expiry time of the indicator, as a time or an ISO 8601
        string. A string without a time zone is in UTC. An expired indicator
        is disabled or deleted, depending on `on_revoke`. Any other value
        yields a `failed` result. Append `?`, as in `expires=valid_until?`,
        when some events lack the field.
    - name: revoked
      type: field
      default: null
      description: |
        Field that is `true` for a revoked indicator, as a boolean or as the
        string `"true"` or `"false"`. A revoked indicator is disabled or
        deleted, depending on `on_revoke`. Any other value yields a `failed`
        result. Append `?` when some events lack the field.
    - name: state
      type: string
      default: "alert"
      description: |
        State of active IOCs and of a new source: `alert` or `backend_alert`,
        and with `allow_blocking=true` also `block` or `quarantine`.
    - name: allow_blocking
      type: bool
      default: false
      description: Allows the `block` and `quarantine` states.
    - name: prune
      type: bool
      default: false
      description: |
        Disables the IOCs of `type` in the source that the input doesn't
        contain. Use it only when every run receives the complete feed.
    - name: max_prune
      type: int
      default: 10
      description: |
        Number of IOCs that pruning may disable in one run regardless of
        `max_prune_share`.
    - name: max_prune_share
      type: float
      default: 0.1
      description: |
        Share of the active IOCs of `type` in the source that pruning may
        disable in one run beyond `max_prune`. A run that would disable more
        stops before any write. `1.0` turns the check off.
    - name: on_revoke
      type: string
      default: "disable"
      description: |
        What happens to expired and revoked indicators: `disable` or `delete`.
    - name: level
      type: string
      default: "high"
      description: |
        Rule level: `critical`, `high`, `medium`, `low`, or `informational`.
        IOCs override the level only when it differs from the source default.
    - name: confidence
      type: string
      default: "strong"
      description: "Rule confidence: `strong`, `moderate`, or `weak`."
    - name: label
      type: string
      default: null
      description: |
        Comment of every IOC, from which HarfangLab builds the alert titles.
        Defaults to `<source>: <value>`.
    - name: parallel
      type: int
      default: 8
      description: |
        Maximum number of concurrent write requests per instance of the
        operator.
    - name: dry_run
      type: bool
      default: false
      description: |
        Reports the actions that a run would take without writing anything,
        not even a missing source.
---

let $api = f"{$url}/api/data/threat_intelligence"
let $headers = {Authorization: f"Token {$token}"}
let $hl_type = {
  domain: "domain_name",
  ip: "ip_dst",
  sha256: "hash",
  sha1: "hash",
  md5: "hash",
  filename: "filename",
  filepath: "filepath",
  url: "url",
}[$type]?
let $hash_length = {sha256: 64, sha1: 40, md5: 32}[$type]?
let $states = ["alert", "backend_alert", "block", "quarantine"] if $allow_blocking else ["alert", "backend_alert"]
let $fields = "id,type,source_id,value,description,comment,global_state,enabled,rule_confidence,rule_level_override"
let $iso8601 = "^[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}([T ][0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2}(:[0-9]{2}([.][0-9]+)?)?(Z|[+-][0-9]{2}:?[0-9]{2})?)?$"
// IDs per bulk request.
let $chunk = 1000

// Normalize and validate each indicator. Conditional chains nest their
// arms, because an arm that yields null would otherwise fall through to the
// next one.
this = {
  input: $value.string().trim(),
  description: $description.string().trim(),
  expires: $expires,
  revoked: $revoked,
}
value = (input.to_lower() if $hl_type in ["domain_name", "hash"]
  else (ip(input).string() if $hl_type == "ip_dst" else input))
expires = expires.trim() if type_kind(expires) == "string" else expires
expires_at = (expires if type_kind(expires) == "time"
  else (time(expires) if type_kind(expires) == "string" and expires.match_regex($iso8601) else null))
revoked = revoked.trim().to_lower() if type_kind(revoked) == "string" else revoked
is_revoked = (false if revoked == null
  else (revoked if type_kind(revoked) == "bool"
  else (revoked == "true" if revoked in ["true", "false"] else null)))
error = ("the value is empty" if (input else "") == ""
  else f"`{input}` is not an IP address" if value == null
  else f"`{input}` is not a valid {$type} hash of {$hash_length} hexadecimal digits" if $hash_length != null and (value.length_chars() != $hash_length or not value.match_regex("^[0-9a-f]+$"))
  else f"expires must be a time or an ISO 8601 string, got `{expires}`" if expires != null and expires_at == null
  else f"revoked must be a boolean, got `{revoked}`" if is_revoked == null
  else null)

if error != null {
  this = {
    value: value if value != null else input,
    type: $type,
    action: "failed",
    ioc_id: null,
    error: error,
  }
} else {
  // Collect the finite input into one event, so that the source is resolved
  // once and the comparison sees the complete input.
  summarize items=collect({
    value: value,
    description: description if description != "" else null,
    retired: is_revoked or (expires_at != null and expires_at < now()),
  })
  strict {
    assert $hl_type != null,
      message=f"type must be one of domain, ip, sha256, sha1, md5, filename, filepath, or url, got `{$type}`"
    assert $state in $states,
      message=f"state must be alert or backend_alert, or block or quarantine with allow_blocking=true, got `{$state}`"
    assert $on_revoke in ["disable", "delete"],
      message=f"on_revoke must be disable or delete, got `{$on_revoke}`"
    assert $level in ["critical", "high", "medium", "low", "informational"],
      message=f"level must be critical, high, medium, low, or informational, got `{$level}`"
    assert $confidence in ["strong", "moderate", "weak"],
      message=f"confidence must be strong, moderate, or weak, got `{$confidence}`"
    assert $parallel >= 1, message=f"parallel must be positive, got {$parallel}"
    assert $max_prune >= 0, message=f"max_prune must not be negative, got {$max_prune}"
    assert $max_prune_share >= 0 and $max_prune_share <= 1,
      message=f"max_prune_share must be between 0 and 1, got {$max_prune_share}"
  }
  where items.length() > 0

  // Look up the source by name. If the listing doesn't contain it, the
  // pagination continues with a request that creates the source, except in a
  // dry run.
  each {
    from_http f"{$api}/IOCSource/?name={$source.encode_url()}&limit=100",
      headers=$headers,
      paginate=(page => {
        url: f"{$api}/IOCSource/",
        method: "post",
        body: {
          name: $source,
          description: "IOCs synchronized by Tenzir",
          enabled: true,
          global_state: $state,
          endpoint_detection: true,
          block_on_agent: false,
          quarantine_on_agent: false,
          rule_level_default: $level,
          rule_confidence_default: $confidence,
        },
      } if not $dry_run and page.count? != null and page.results.where(s => s.name == $source).length() == 0 else null) {
      read_json raw=true
    }
    source = (results? else [this]).where(s => s.name? == $source).first()
    summarize source=first(source)
    this = {
      items: $this.items,
      source_id: source.id?,
      source_level: source.rule_level_default?,
    }
  }

  // Read the IOCs of this type in the source once, with only the fields that
  // the comparison needs. The Manager returns the next page as a path. The
  // run stops if the pages don't add up to the count of the listing. Rows of
  // another type, source, or hash algorithm are dropped, so that neither the
  // comparison nor pruning touches them.
  if source_id == null {
    existing = []
  } else {
    each {
      from_http f"{$api}/IOCRule/?source_id={$this.source_id}&type={$hl_type}&ordering=id&limit=10000&fields={$fields}",
        headers=$headers,
        paginate=(page => (page.next if page.next.starts_with("http") else f"{$url}{page.next}") if page.next? != null else null) {
        read_json raw=true
      }
      summarize expected=max(count), received=sum(results.length()), pages=collect(results)
      strict {
        assert received == expected,
          message=f"the listing of source `{$source}` returned {received} of {expected} IOCs, so the run stops before any write"
      }
      unroll pages
      unroll pages
      this = pages
      where type == $hl_type and source_id == $this.source_id
      where $hash_length == null or value.length_chars() == $hash_length
      summarize existing=collect(this)
      this = {...$this, existing: existing else []}
    }
  }

  // Join the input with the existing IOCs by their lowercase value. The
  // Manager may hold IP addresses in another form than the canonical one.
  this = {
    source_id: source_id,
    source_level: source_level,
    rows: [
      ...items.map(x => {key: x.value.to_lower(), desired: x, current: null}),
      ...existing.map(x => {
        key: ((ip(x.value).string() if $hl_type == "ip_dst" else null) else x.value).to_lower(),
        desired: null,
        current: x,
      }),
    ],
  }
  unroll rows
  summarize key=rows.key,
    desired=collect(rows.desired),
    current=first(rows.current),
    source_id=first(source_id),
    source_level=first(source_level)

  // Resolve duplicate input rows: an active row wins over a retired one, and
  // the first value and description in sort order win.
  active = desired.where(x => not x.retired)
  listed = desired.length() > 0
  retired = listed and active.length() == 0
  desired = active if active.length() > 0 else desired
  value = desired.map(x => x.value).sort().first() if listed else current.value
  target = $state if listed and not retired else "disabled"
  want = {
    description: desired.map(x => x.description).where(x => x != null).sort().first(),
    comment: $label if $label != null else f"{$source}: {value}",
    rule_confidence: $confidence,
    rule_level_override: $level if source_level != $level else null,
  }
  state_changed = current != null and (current.global_state != target
    or current.enabled != (target != "disabled"))
  content_changed = current != null and (
    (want.description else "") != (current.description else "")
    or (want.comment else "") != (current.comment else "")
    or want.rule_confidence != current.rule_confidence
    or want.rule_level_override != current.rule_level_override)

  // Decide what to do with every indicator:
  // - create: POST of a new IOC.
  // - state: a bulk state change, followed by a PATCH if `patch` is true.
  // - prune: a bulk state change of an IOC that the input doesn't contain.
  // - patch: PATCH of an IOC whose content alone differs.
  // - delete: a bulk deletion of a revoked or expired IOC.
  plan = ("ignore" if not listed and (not $prune or not state_changed)
    else "prune" if not listed
    else "skipped" if current == null and retired
    else "create" if current == null
    else "delete" if retired and $on_revoke == "delete"
    else "unchanged" if retired and not state_changed
    else "state" if state_changed
    else "patch" if content_changed
    else "unchanged")
  where plan != "ignore"
  this = {
    value: value,
    plan: plan,
    patch: plan == "state" and not retired and content_changed,
    target: target,
    want: want,
    ioc_id: current.id?,
    active: current != null and current.global_state != "disabled" and current.enabled != false,
    source_id: source_id,
  }

  // Check the prune limit across all indicators before any write.
  summarize rows=collect(this)
  pruned = rows.where(r => r.plan == "prune").length()
  active = rows.where(r => r.active).length()
  strict {
    assert $dry_run or pruned <= $max_prune or pruned <= $max_prune_share * active,
      message=f"pruning would disable {pruned} of {active} active IOCs of source `{$source}`, more than max_prune={$max_prune} and max_prune_share={$max_prune_share}, so the run stops before any write"
  }
  unroll rows
  this = rows

  // Change states and delete IOCs in bulk requests of up to `$chunk` IDs per
  // target, before any other write.
  if not $dry_run and plan in ["state", "prune", "delete"] {
    enumerate index
    batch = floor(index / $chunk)
    kind = "delete" if plan == "delete" else "state"
    summarize kind, target, batch, rows=collect(this)
    if kind == "delete" {
      each parallel=$parallel {
        from_http f"{$api}/IOCSource/{$this.rows[0].source_id}/items/",
          method="delete",
          headers=$headers,
          body={ids: $this.rows.map(r => r.ioc_id)},
          error_field=error {
          read_json raw=true
        }
        // The Manager may answer without a body, from which `from_http` emits
        // no event, so `summarize` makes up the one result.
        summarize error=first(error?)
        this = {rows: $this.rows, error: error.string()}
      }
    } else {
      each parallel=$parallel {
        from_http f"{$api}/IOCRule/update/",
          headers=$headers,
          body={
            rule_ids: $this.rows.map(r => r.ioc_id),
            global_state: $this.target,
            enabled: $this.target != "disabled",
          },
          error_field=error {
          read_json raw=true
        }
        summarize error=first(error?)
        this = {rows: $this.rows, error: error.string()}
      }
    }
    unroll rows
    this = {...rows, error: error}
  }
  // Wait for the bulk requests to finish.
  summarize rows=collect(this)
  unroll rows
  this = rows

  if not $dry_run and plan == "create" {
    each parallel=$parallel {
      from_http f"{$api}/IOCRule/",
        headers=$headers,
        body={
          source_id: $this.source_id,
          type: $hl_type,
          value: $this.value,
          hl_status: "stable",
          global_state: $state,
          enabled: true,
          ...$this.want,
        },
        error_field=error {
        read_json raw=true
      }
      this = {
        value: $this.value,
        type: $type,
        action: "created" if error? == null else "failed",
        ioc_id: id?,
        error: error?.string(),
      }
    }
  } else if not $dry_run and (plan == "patch" or (patch and error? == null)) {
    each parallel=$parallel {
      from_http f"{$api}/IOCRule/{$this.ioc_id}/",
        method="patch",
        headers=$headers,
        body=$this.want,
        error_field=error {
        read_json raw=true
      }
      this = {
        value: $this.value,
        type: $type,
        action: "updated" if error? == null else "failed",
        ioc_id: $this.ioc_id,
        error: error?.string(),
      }
    }
  } else {
    this = {
      value: value,
      type: $type,
      action: ("failed" if error? != null
        else "created" if plan == "create"
        else "updated" if plan == "patch" or (plan == "state" and target != "disabled")
        else "disabled" if plan in ["state", "prune"]
        else "deleted" if plan == "delete"
        else plan),
      ioc_id: ioc_id,
      error: error?,
    }
  }
}
